# Services: always neverthrow

Service methods must return `Result` or `ResultAsync` from `neverthrow`. Do not throw for expected failures (auth, validation, PocketBase errors).

For **where** external APIs / debrid providers live and how they register on `Services`, see [`services-external-apis`](services-external-apis.mdc).

## Patterns

- Extend `Service` from `$lib/server/base.service`.
- Prefer `ResultAsync` for async work.
- Map PocketBase promises with `fromPb` from `$lib/server/result` so errors become typed `AppError`.
- Every `AppError` must include a unique, grep-able `code` (via `ERROR_CODE` + `panic` / `httpError` / `configError`). Never invent ad-hoc `{ kind, message }` objects without a code.
- Surface errors to clients with `formatAppError` so the code stays visible.
- Callers handle `.match` / `.map` / `.mapErr` — never swallow errors with empty catches.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — throws / bare Promise
async login(email: string, password: string) {
  return this.pocketbase.collection('users').authWithPassword(email, password);
}

// ✅ GOOD — ResultAsync + fromPb
import { fromPb } from './result';

login(email: string, password: string) {
  return fromPb(
    this.pocketbase.collection('users').authWithPassword(email, password)
  );
}
```

## Do not

- Return raw promises that reject for domain errors
- Use try/catch only to rethrow untyped errors when `fromPb` / `ResultAsync.fromPromise` fits
- Mix throwing APIs with Result-returning methods in the same service without a clear boundary
